nseUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gwangju_Dong-gu_Election_Commission.jpg"}},{"id":"gwangju_jeungsimsa_temple","areaId":"gwangju","name":"Jeungsimsa Temple","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":35.1219,"lng":126.9722},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"gwangju_jeungsimsa_temple","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["jeungsimsatemple","gwangju"],"summary":"Jeungsimsa Temple, one of Gwangju’s main Buddhist temples, is located at the western foot of Mudeungsan Mountain. Important cultural artifacts are preserved on the grounds. Climbing up the temple is quite easy. You can walk along the trail with an atmosphere in a quiet stillness. Jeungsimsa operates temple stay programs for tourists.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gwangju","names":{"ja":"證心寺","zh":"證心寺"},"photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/%EC%A6%9D%EC%8B%AC%EC%82%AC_%EC%A0%84%EA%B2%BD.JPG/1280px-%EC%A6%9D%EC%8B%AC%EC%82%AC_%EC%A0%84%EA%B2%BD.JPG","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/%EC%A6%9D%EC%8B%AC%EC%82%AC_%EC%A0%84%EA%B2%BD.JPG/500px-%EC%A6%9D%EC%8B%AC%EC%82%AC_%EC%A0%84%EA%B2%BD.JPG","w":1200,"h":800,"author":"Dalgial","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%EC%A6%9D%EC%8B%AC%EC%82%AC_%EC%A0%84%EA%B2%BD.JPG"}},{"id":"gwangju_gwangju_confucian_school","areaId":"gwangju","name":"Gwangju Confucian School","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":35.1458,"lng":126.9093},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"gwangju_gwangju_confucian_school","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["gwangjuconfucianschool","gwangju"],"summary":"The Gwangju Confucian School, which played a key role in Confucian education during the Joseon Dynasty (1329–1910) and served as a kind of national university at the time, today offers a “Confucian university” program through which participants can experience diverse aspects of traditional culture.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gwangju","names":{"ja":"広州郷校"},"photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Gwangju_Hyanggyo_in_Hanam_City.jpg/1280px-Gwangju_Hyanggyo_in_Hanam_City.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Gwangju_Hyanggyo_in_Hanam_City.jpg/500px-Gwangju_Hyanggyo_in_Hanam_City.jpg","w":1200,"h":675,"author":"Qkqhrhkdtn","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gwangju_Hyanggyo_in_Hanam_City.jpg"}},{"id":"gwangju_wv_the_traditional_culture_center","areaId":"gwangju","name":"The Traditional Culture Center","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":35.1336,"lng":126.9521},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"gwangju_wv_the_traditional_culture_center","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["thetraditionalculturecenter","gwangju"],"summary":"The center is near the entrance of Jeungsimsa Temple, at the foot of Mudeungsan Mountain. At the center, masters who have been designated as intangible cultural properties teach the public about traditional culture: Pansori (traditional Korean folk opera); Janggu (traditional drumming technique); Gayageum (traditional Korean zither). Performances are also held to demonstrate such elements of tradi","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gwangju"},{"id":"gwangju_yangdong_market","areaId":"gwangju","name":"Yangdong Market","category":"market","tags":["markets","food"],"location":{"lat":35.154,"lng":126.901},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"gwangju_yangdong_market","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["yangdongmarket","gwangju"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},null],"note":"Closed Sun; Typical hours — check the official site"},"bestLight":"morning","summary":"Since 2005, the river area has been undergoing a surprising facelift, stretching from Gwangju's most famous food, clothing and furniture market, Yangdong Market, all the way out of the city in a southeasterly direction. The river edge is beautifully lit at night, and with its colored lights and shopping areas nearby, is rapidly becoming a symbol of Gwangju - the City of Light and Culture.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gwangju"},{"id":"gwangju_wv_gwangju_student_independence_movement_memorial_h","areaId":"gwangju","name":"Gwangju Student Independence Movement Memorial Hall","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":35.1405,"lng":126.8653},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"gwangju_wv_gwangju_student_independence_movement_memorial_h","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://gsim.gen.go.kr/en/index.php","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["gwangjustudentindependencemovementmemorialhall","gwangju"],"summary":"This monument is in the geographical middle of the city. Not widely known, and requires a taxi ride to get to, this monument is rather large and situated in a very quiet park atop a hill. The monument commemorates the student uprising against Japanese Imperialism in the early 1900s. The Park includes an impressive museum with detailed representations of the time. At times English tours are availab","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gwangju"},{"id":"gwangju_wv_pung_am_district","areaId":"gwangju","name":"Pung-am District","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":35.1295,"lng":126.8814},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"gwangju_wv_pung_am_district","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["pungamdistrict","gwangju"],"summary":"Within Pungam is the World Cup Stadium (월드컵 경기장), connected to the Lotte Outlet Mall. A short walk from the stadium is the Pungam Reservoir, which has fountains, statues, and a walking path. If you enjoy hiking, you can also take an easy hike around Geumdangsan Mountain, which encircles the Pungam residential area. Starting from an Oriental medicine hospital, Wongwangdae hospital, the hike takes o","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gwangju"},{"id":"gwangju_wv_ori_tang","areaId":"gwangju","name":"Ori-tang","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":35.1614,"lng":126.9059},"visitMinutes":75,"photoSeed":"gwangju_wv_ori_tang","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["oritanggwangju","gwangju"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"Gwangju duck stew is a special cuisine which is not easy to taste in the other parts of South Korea. Gwangju and Jeolla Province’s duck stew contains chili pepper powder, water parsley, and roasted perilla seeds to thicken the dish. It served with a rice porridge made with jujube, glutinous rice, ginseng, chestnut, and so forth. It contains chili pepper powder, but it is the right amount of spicy ","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gwangju"},{"id":"gwangju_wv_sangchu_twigim","areaId":"gwangju","name":"Sangchu-Twigim","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":35.1483,"lng":126.8486},"visitMinutes":75,"photoSeed":"gwangju_wv_sangchu_twigim","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["sangchutwigimgwangju","gwangju"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"It is an unused concept. It is pretty similar to Ssam (eat something wrapped in leaves of lettuce), but the contents are deep-fried food or something like fritters. Pick the fried food, dipped in soy sauce, wrapped in leaves of lettuce, and devour it. It sounds weird but, the leaves of lettuce help to get rid of greasiness of fried food, and it is a sublime combination of flavors. The dedicated st","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gwangju"},{"id":"gwangju_wv_yuk_jeon","areaId":"gwangju","name":"Yuk-jeon","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":35.14554,"lng":126.91436},"visitMinutes":75,"photoSeed":"gwangju_wv_yuk_jeon","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["yukjeongwangju","gwangju"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"They slice the beef thinly, dip it in an egg mixture and wheat flour and sear it lightly. You can eat it wrapped in leaves of lettuce or mixed with green onion salad. It is somewhat expensive but worth a splurge.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gwangju"},{"id":"gwangju_wv_hwangsolchon","areaId":"gwangju","name":"Hwangsolchon","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":35.1471,"lng":126.9143},"visitMinutes":75,"photoSeed":"gwangju_wv_hwangsolchon","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["hwa